  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This one won't be a terribly high priority I'm sure, but I noticed something odd when I visited a world called Waterfall HD today. It seemed like something was off about my voice. I soon realized what the issue was... My voice sounded completely flat, while everyone else in the world who was talking had a heavy echo / reverb applied to them as if they were in a cavern, which they were. I noticed that not having this effect also applied to my voice felt wrong. \n\nSo I wondered if it would be possible to add echo to your voice to match the VR environment? This would obviously have to be tweaked carefully as hearing your own voice returned back to you can make it hard for you to speak. I'm not sure how much of a delay or attenuation you need to avoid this issue, but if it were possible to make this work, it would make the vr environments that much more immersive!",
